From: Pi4 Xen Lab <pi4-xen-lab@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] bootstrap: accept dependencies prepared by the build system

BitBake fetches immutable revisions for the build dependencies before running
tasks without network access. Skip upstream's developer/test submodule update
when those dependencies have already been prepared. The normal upstream
bootstrap behavior is unchanged unless explicitly requested.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [build-system integration]

--- a/bootstrap.conf
+++ b/bootstrap.conf
@@ -59,9 +59,11 @@ if test -n "$SUBMODULE_NOFETCH"; then
   git_options="--no-fetch"
 fi
 
-for mod in $required_submodules; do
-  git submodule update --init $git_options $mod
-done
+if test "${GNUTLS_BOOTSTRAP_OFFLINE:-no}" != yes; then
+  for mod in $required_submodules; do
+    git submodule update --init $git_options $mod
+  done
+fi
 
 # This check needs to be done before actual import.
 TMP_GNULIB_SRCDIR="${GNULIB_SRCDIR:-gnulib}"
